course: dictionary
lesson: 7435
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. Pollock is one of them. Context, the words around it, tells you which meaning the writer means. «Fish fingers are usually white fish such as cod, pollock or haddock» is about a sea fish, because cod and haddock are fish too.
explain: «Jackson Pollock laid huge canvases on the floor and dripped and flung paint» is about a person. Jackson is a first name, and a capital P on Pollock tells you it is a surname, the family name of a painter. Ask yourself: is this a thing, or a person?
explain: Always check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. Put «a sea fish» in place of pollock in the fish sentence: it still makes sense. Put «a sea fish» into the painter sentence: it does not, so the word must mean a painter there.
fact: Pollock is a sea fish of the North Atlantic, related to the cod.
fact: Pollock is often eaten as fish fingers or fish and chips.
fact: Pollock is also a surname: Jackson Pollock was an American painter.
fact: Jackson Pollock was famous for dripping and splashing paint on large canvases.
fact: Context clues, such as fish and chips or Jackson, show which meaning of a word the writer intends.
exercise: In «Fish fingers are usually white fish such as cod, pollock or haddock», what is pollock? | A famous painter | A kind of breadcrumb | A frozen pizza topping | *A sea fish
exercise: In «Jackson Pollock laid huge canvases on the floor», what is Pollock? | A hard floor tile | A sea fish | *A surname, the name of a painter | A type of canvas
exercise: Which clue tells you pollock is the fish, not the painter? | American and painter | Jackson and canvases | Large paintings on a floor | *Fish fingers and fish and chips
test: Pollock is a fish related to which other fish? | *Cod | Goldfish | Trout | Salmon
test: Jackson Pollock was famous for what kind of painting? | *Dripping and splashing paint on large canvases | Smooth, careful portraits | Photographs of cats | Carved stone statues
exam: In «Alaska pollock fillets were on sale», what does pollock mean? | A kind of cheese | *A sea fish | A famous painter | A large town
